<div class="wrap">

  <header class="masthead">
    {# One element, relocated by JS when embedded. Duplicating it would inline
       the whole data URI twice and add ~140KB to the page for nothing. #}
    {% if logo %}<img class="brand" id="brand" src="{{ logo }}" alt="{{ title }}">{% endif %}
    <div class="masthead-text">
      <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
      <p>Employment change by industry, from the BLS Current Employment Statistics survey</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="controls">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="base">Base period</label>
      <select id="base"></select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="horizon">Comparison period</label>
      <select id="horizon"></select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="level">Display level</label>
      <select id="level"></select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="metric">Colour metric</label>
      <div class="seg" id="metric" role="group" aria-label="Colour metric">
        <button type="button" data-metric="abs" aria-pressed="true">Absolute</button>
        <button type="button" data-metric="pct" aria-pressed="false">Percent</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="palette">Palette</label>
      <select id="palette">
        <option value="accessible">Accessible red↔blue</option>
        <option value="classic">Classic red↔green</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="q">Highlight industry</label>
      <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Type to highlight…" autocomplete="off">
    </div>
    <div class="field actions">
      <button type="button" id="up" title="Go up one level (Esc)">↑ Up</button>
      <button type="button" id="link" title="Copy a link to this exact view">Copy link</button>
      <button type="button" id="csv" title="Download the current view as CSV">CSV</button>
      <button type="button" id="png" title="Download the current view as PNG">PNG</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <nav class="crumbs" id="crumbs" aria-label="Industry hierarchy"></nav>

  <h2 class="chart-title" id="charttitle"></h2>
  <p class="lagnote" id="lagnote" hidden></p>
  <p class="lagnote" id="nomatch" hidden></p>
  <p class="lagnote" id="levelnote" hidden></p>

  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <svg id="treemap" role="img" aria-label="Treemap of employment change by industry. Tile area is the absolute change; colour is the signed change. Use Tab to move between industries, Enter to drill in, Escape to go up."></svg>
    <p class="empty" id="empty" hidden></p>
  </div>

  <div class="legend-row">
    <div class="legend">
      <div class="cap" id="legendcap"></div>
      <div class="bar" id="legendbar"></div>
      <div class="ends"><span id="legendlo"></span><span>0</span><span id="legendhi"></span></div>
      <div class="nodatakey"><span class="swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span> No data published for this period</div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer-brand" id="footer-brand">
      <div class="stamp" id="stamp"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="stamp footnote" style="text-align:left;margin-top:14px">
    Tile area is the <strong>absolute</strong> change in employees in both colour modes — sizing by
    percent would let a very small industry outweigh Food Services. Colour is symmetric around zero,
    so a loss and a gain of equal size read at equal intensity.{{ export_note }}
    CES publishes only some children for many parents, so the tiles at a level are not a complete
    partition of it — every tile is the value CES actually reports, never scaled or padded to make
    the pieces add up. Three roll-ups that would <em>double-count</em> their own same-level
    components — <em>Health care</em>, <em>Specialty trade contractors</em> and <em>Motor vehicles
    and parts</em> — are hidden for that reason; append <code>&amp;dupes=1</code> to show them.
  </p>
{% if source_url %}  <p class="stamp footnote credit" style="text-align:left">
    Built and maintained by {{ source_publisher }}. Rebuilt from the BLS API after each
    Employment Situation release. Full methodology, sources and answers to common questions:
    <a href="{{ source_url }}">{{ source_title }}</a>.
  </p>
{% endif %}</div>

<div id="tip" role="tooltip"></div>

<script>const PAYLOAD = {{ payload }};</script>
<script>{{ js }}</script>
